Yes — for antialiasing of horizontal lines, a practical approach is to detect them after rasterizing and edge extraction, then filter by near-zero slope.

For example, in Mathematica:

```wl
img = Import["https://i.sstatic.net/ZObmf.jpg"];
rasImg = Rasterize[img, RasterSize -> 100];
edges = EdgeDetect[rasImg, 2, 0.022, "StraightEdges" -> 0.11];
lines = ImageLines[edges, 0.03, "Segmented" -> True];

horizontalQ[expr_, angle_] := Abs[ArcTan[Abs[expr[[2, 2]] - expr[[1, 2]]]/Max[1, Abs[expr[[2, 1]] - expr[[1, 1]]]]]] <= angle;

horLines = Select[lines, horizontalQ[First[#], 0.01 Pi] &];
Graphics[Line /@ horLines]
```

