pow = {0, 1, 2, 3, 4};

prm = Permutations[pow];
val = Inner[Power, num, #, Plus] & /@ prm;

maxIndex = First@Flatten@Position[val, Max[val]];
{prm[[maxIndex]], val[[maxIndex]]}
```

This returns the maximizing permutation and its value:

- permutation: `{0, 4, 1, 3, 2}`
- maximum sum: `289091/126000 ≈ 2.294373016`

So your proposed arrangement is correct.

