Manipulate[
 Column[{
   Round[xguide, 2],
   Plot[PrimePi[x], {x, 0, 200},
    PlotPoints -> 200,
    ImageSize -> 600,
    Epilog -> {
      Gray,
      Line[{{Round[xguide[[1]], 2], -1000}, {Round[xguide[[1]], 2], 1000}}],
      Line[{{-1000, Round[xguide[[2]], 2]}, {1000, Round[xguide[[2]], 2]}}]
    }]
   }],
 {{xguide, {20, 20}}, Locator, Appearance -> None}
]
```

This gives draggable horizontal/vertical guides, and `Round[..., 2]` can be changed for snapping.

Use `Epilog` to draw the lines, and control their positions with a `Locator` in `Manipulate`.

Example for multiple horizontal lines:

```mathematica
