Yes — you can nest `Table` so the `j`-dependent quantities are computed once per `j`, not once per `k`.

For example:

```mathematica
Table[
  Table[
    p = test[[i, j, 1]];
    q = test[[i, j, 2]];
    r = Cross[p, q];
    mat = Orthogonalize[{p, q, r}];
    Table[
      mat.SeparationVector[p, test[[i, k, 1]], 2],
      {k, 5}
    ],
    {j, 5}
  ],
  {i, 10}
]
```

This preserves the reuse you want:
- `p, q, r, mat` are computed once per `j`
- only the final `k`-loop depends on `k`

