If you mean a tangent line that “slides” along a curve, parameterize the curve and draw the line at the moving point.

For a 2D curve {x(t), y(t)}, the tangent line at t0 is:
{ x(t0), y(t0) } + s { x’(t0), y’(t0) }

In Mathematica, you can animate it with ParametricPlot:

```wl
curve[t_] := {t, t^2};
Manipulate[
 Show[
  ParametricPlot[curve[u], {u, -2, 2}],
  ParametricPlot[
   curve[t0] + s*D[curve[t], t] /. t -> t0,
   {s, -2, 2}, PlotStyle -> Red
  ]
 ],
 {t0, -2, 2}
]
```

