Use a 2D `ContourPlot` for the circle, then lift its lines into 3D by appending `z = 0`, and combine with your `ContourPlot3D`.

```mathematica
Show[
 ContourPlot3D[
  {x^2 + y^2 == z, 2 y == z, x^2 + (y - 1/2)^2 == 1},
  {x, -2, 2}, {y, -0.5, 1}, {z, 0, 2},
  ContourStyle -> Opacity[.3]
 ],
 Graphics3D[
