A `PlotMarker` won’t help much here because its size is tied to plot/absolute scaling, not directly to your data’s uncertainty.

A better approach is to use `ErrorListPlot` and replace the error bars with a custom graphic, e.g. a `Disk` whose radius is computed from the error value:

```wl
Needs["ErrorBarPlots`"]

data = {
  {{1, 1}, ErrorBar[0.2, 0.3]},
  {{2, 2}, ErrorBar[0.2, 0.3]},
  {{3, 4}, ErrorBar[0.2, 0.5]},
  {{4, 8}, ErrorBar[1, 2]}
};

ErrorListPlot[
  data,
  ErrorBarFunction -> Function[{coords, errs},
    {Opacity[0.2], Disk[coords, (errs[[2, 2]] - errs[[2, 1]])/2]}
  ]
]
```

