Your function is using the built-in symbol K as if it were your kernel function.

In Mathematica, K is reserved as a generic summation index symbol, so `K[t_] := ...` does not behave as you expect. That’s why the parallel evaluation ends up with empty graphics.

Fix: use a different name, like `k`:

```mathematica
k[t_] := 1.078222*Exp[-(t^2/0.273800)];

KSmoothTest[vy_, b_] := Block[{n, weights},
  n = Length[vy];
  weights = Table[k[i/b], {i, 0, Length[vy] - 1}];
  Table[
    Sum[weights[[Abs[i - j] + 1]]*vy[[j]], {j, 1, n}]/
    Sum[weights[[Abs[i - j] + 1]], {j, 1, n}],
    {i, 1, n}
  ]
];
```

Then `ParallelTable[...]` should work properly.

