In Mathematica, symbols defined inside `Begin["`Private`"]` stay private and won’t be visible as exported package functions.

You need to declare public symbols in the `BeginPackage[...]` section first, for example:

```mathematica
BeginPackage["mypackage`"]

getColumn::usage = "getColumn[data, branch] ...";
RemoveMissing::usage = "RemoveMissing[data] ...";

Begin["`Private`"]

getColumn[data_, branch_List] := Module[{pos},
  pos = Position[data, #][[1, 2]] & /@ branch;
  data[[All, pos]]
];

RemoveMissing[data_] := DeleteCases[data, {date_, val_} /; !NumberQ[val]];

End[]
EndPackage[]
```

Also, the package file name should usually match the package context, e.g. `mypackage.m` for `mypackage``.

