If you mean “write to the nth line” in an existing file, Mathematica generally can’t efficiently overwrite an arbitrary line in place. `OpenWrite`/`OpenAppend` streams can’t be repositioned to rewrite earlier parts safely.

The usual solution is:

1. Read the original file line by line.
2. Write a new temporary file.
3. Replace only the nth line while copying the rest.
4. Rename the temp file over the original.

Example:

```mathematica
replaceNthLine[file_String, n_Integer, new_] := Module[
  {in = OpenRead[file], out = OpenWrite[file <> ".tmp"], line, i = 1},
  While[(line = Read[in, Record]) =!= EndOfFile,
    WriteString[out, If[i == n, new, line] <> "\n"];
    i++
  ];
  Close /@ {in, out};
  CopyFile[file <> ".tmp", file, OverwriteTarget -> True];
  DeleteFile[file <> ".tmp"];
]
```

