Since your example has Dimensions[M] == {10, 9}, it is an overdetermined system. In the resolved thread, the key observation was:

- MatrixRank[M] == 9
- MatrixRank[M[[1 ;; 9]]] == 9

So you can reduce it to a square 9×9 system and use Cramer’s rule for individual components:

```wl
M = M[[1 ;; 9]];
b = b[[1 ;; 9]];
det = Det[M];

solvefor[i_] := Module[{B},
  B = M;
  B[[All, i]] = b;
  Det[B]/det
]
```

Then `solvefor[1]` gives x1, etc.

This is efficient if you only need selected components, since it avoids computing the full solution vector.

