Use `Partition` to grab adjacent point pairs, then build one linear segment per pair and wrap them in `Piecewise`.

If your data are values at consecutive x-positions, e.g. `{1,1,1,0,0,1,1}`, you can do:

```mathematica
createPiecewise[l_List] := Piecewise[
  MapIndexed[
    With[{pos = First[#2], y1 = First[#], y2 = Last[#]},
      {y1 (1 + pos - x) + y2 (x - pos), pos <= x < pos + 1}
    ] &,
    Partition[l, 2, 1]
  ]
]
```

