This is usually a context/path issue.

When a package is loaded, unqualified symbols inside `Begin["`Private`"]` can still resolve to symbols already on `$ContextPath`. So `function1` may end up referring to the public `Test1\`function1` instead of `Test1\`Private\`function1`, especially after reloading.

Fix it by explicitly qualifying the private definition:

```mathematica
BeginPackage["Test1`"];
Begin["`Private`"];
Test1`Private`function1[x_] := x
End[];
EndPackage[];
```

Or clear the symbol before defining it:

```mathematica
BeginPackage["Test1`"];
Remove[function1];
Begin["`Private`"];
function1[x_] := x
End[];
EndPackage[];
```

If needed, reset with `Remove["Test1`*"]` before reloading.

