If you want to fit ODE coefficients, use `NMinimize`/`FindFit` around a numerical ODE solve.

Typical pattern:

```wl
data = (* {t_i, y_i} points *);

sol[c1_, c2_] := NDSolveValue[
  {y'[t] == c1 y[t] + c2 t, y[0] == y0},
  y, {t, tmin, tmax}
];

obj[c1_, c2_] := Total[(sol[c1, c2] /@ data[[All, 1]] - data[[All, 2]])^2];

NMinimize[{obj[c1, c2], bounds}, {c1, c2}]
```

For more parameters, this is the same idea.

If the ODE is stiff or hard to solve, use `NDSolveValue` carefully with numeric-only functions, as in the earlier note: keep everything numeric, and consider `Method -> "StiffnessSwitching"`.

